         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/7319a2d0-4dfc-43b3-bf4c-5894bd722e83,1792781611519/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C147%2C4870%2C2739%29%3B' alt='A man wearing a baseball helmet and a blue navy jersey spelling &quot;Rays&quot; is shown running.' width='620' height='349' title='Tampa Bay Rays&apos; Liam Hicks rounds the bases after hitting a two-run home run in the third inning of a baseball game against the Atlanta Braves, Tuesday, Sept. 8, 2026, in Atlanta. (AP Photo/Colin Hubbard)'/><p>In just his second big league season, Toronto catcher Liam Hicks will make his World Series debut when the Tampa Rays take on the Milwaukee Brewers for Game 1 at 8 p.m. ET Friday.</p>]]></description>
